00:10:59,967 --> 00:11:00,933
- [Crow] Hey, your Playboy
air freshener thing

252
00:11:00,933 --> 00:11:02,000
dropped on the floor.

253
00:11:03,100 --> 00:11:06,700
- [Mike] Hey, back at ya pal.

254
00:11:08,867 --> 00:11:11,667
- [Tom] I hope he puts in
his eight track of Aqualung.

255
00:11:11,667 --> 00:11:13,100
- [Watney] What the hell's the
matter with the car, Kevin?

256
00:11:13,100 --> 00:11:14,367
Whoa, whoa, keep it on the road.

257
00:11:14,367 --> 00:11:15,800
- [Crow] It's just the
stagehand's last day.

258
00:11:18,467 --> 00:11:20,633
- [Tom] Once I get
up to 90 it'll stop.

259
00:11:20,633 --> 00:11:24,033
When time traveling, always
wear your seat belts.

260
00:11:24,033 --> 00:11:25,567
- [Mike] You think
there's any chance

261
00:11:25,567 --> 00:11:28,167
Barney Rubble there could
go through the windshield?

262
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:34,067
- [Crow] Sorry folks, we
simply could not afford

263
00:11:34,067 --> 00:11:35,967
to have special effects.

264
00:11:35,967 --> 00:11:39,400
(singing a tune)

265
00:11:39,400 --> 00:11:40,867
- [Tom] Oh, they're in Ishtar.

266
00:11:40,867 --> 00:11:43,233
- [Mike] Todo, I have a feeling
this isn't the red onion.

267
00:11:43,233 --> 00:11:46,467
- [Crow] He's a mouth
breather, that one.

268
00:11:48,833 --> 00:11:52,767
- [Watney] Cabot,
Cabot, you okay?

269
00:11:52,767 --> 00:11:54,033
Cabot, speak to me, you alright?

270
00:11:54,033 --> 00:11:55,300
Cabot, what the hell's going on?

271
00:12:00,100 --> 00:12:01,833
Where the hell's the car?

272
00:12:01,833 --> 00:12:02,700
- [Actor] I thought you had it.

273
00:12:07,933 --> 00:12:10,200
- [Crow] We have worm sign.

274
00:12:13,600 --> 00:12:14,867
- I can't believe it.

275
00:12:14,867 --> 00:12:16,167
- [Tom] The things I can
do with my spinal graft.

276
00:12:16,167 --> 00:12:17,100
- I can't believe it.

277
00:12:17,100 --> 00:12:20,733
I'm back, I am back, I am back.

278
00:12:20,733 --> 00:12:22,167
- [Tom] And better than ever.

279
00:12:22,167 --> 00:12:23,400
- [Watney] Back where?

280
00:12:23,400 --> 00:12:25,133
- [Talena] This is
where Talena lives.

281
00:12:25,133 --> 00:12:26,400
- [Watney] Who's Talena?

282
00:12:26,400 --> 00:12:28,000
- [Cabot] Talena,
my girl, my love.

283
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:28,933
This is the plante
of Gor, Gor, Gor!

284
00:12:28,933 --> 00:12:30,533
- [Watley] What the hell's Gor?

285
00:12:30,533 --> 00:12:32,233
- [Tom] It's the hell here.

286
00:12:33,833 --> 00:12:35,433
- Listen Cabot, what
are you talking about?

287
00:12:35,433 --> 00:12:36,733
Where the hell are we?

288
00:12:36,733 --> 00:12:38,733
What's going on here, Cabot?

289
00:12:38,733 --> 00:12:39,600
- [Crow] Shh, I'm acting.

290
00:12:39,600 --> 00:12:40,567
- I must go to Koruba.

291
00:12:40,567 --> 00:12:41,867
- What?

292
00:12:41,867 --> 00:12:42,700
- Koruba!

293
00:12:42,700 --> 00:12:43,900
- [Watney] Same to you.

294
00:12:43,900 --> 00:12:45,333
Cabot, Cabot, listen
to me, what's going on,

295
00:12:45,333 --> 00:12:46,867
what happened last night?

296
00:12:46,867 --> 00:12:49,333
(chanting "kill him")

297
00:12:49,333 --> 00:12:51,100
Cabot, listen, would
you speak to me?

298
00:12:51,100 --> 00:12:52,867
I want to go home right
now, alright, Cabot?

299
00:12:52,867 --> 00:12:54,400
Where you going?

300
00:12:54,400 --> 00:12:56,000
No, no, wait, Cabot, show me
what the hell's going on here.

301
00:12:56,000 --> 00:13:00,233
- [Tom] Cabot, no one would see
if you killed him right now.

302
00:13:00,233 --> 00:13:01,500
- [Crow] They'd probably
give him a free drink

303
00:13:01,500 --> 00:13:02,300
at the Pullman.

304
00:13:03,500 --> 00:13:05,033
- [Watney] Cabot,
would you wait up?

305
00:13:06,733 --> 00:13:08,433
- [Tom] Hey, Cabot.

306
00:13:09,300 --> 00:13:10,667
I'm a bad boy.

307
00:13:12,067 --> 00:13:13,933
- [Watney] Cabot,
it's getting hot.

308
00:13:13,933 --> 00:13:15,200
- [Mike] This would be
a good drinking game.

309
00:13:15,200 --> 00:13:16,667
Every time he says Cabot
you could take a drink.

310
00:13:16,667 --> 00:13:20,400
- [watney] Cabot, Cabot, Cabot,

311
00:13:20,400 --> 00:13:22,200
can we just hold it a minute?

312
00:13:22,200 --> 00:13:24,533
- [Tom] Shh, he's conducting
the Flight of the Bumble Bee.

313
00:13:24,533 --> 00:13:26,867
- [Cabot] We're getting close.

314
00:13:26,867 --> 00:13:27,800
- [Watney] Getting
close to where?

315
00:13:27,800 --> 00:13:29,433
- [Crow] The Perkins on 494.

316
00:13:29,433 --> 00:13:30,667
- [Watney] Koruba?

317
00:13:30,667 --> 00:13:32,800
Hey, are there any
women on Koruba?

318
00:13:32,800 --> 00:13:34,500
- [Tom] Yeah, and
they'll reject you too.

319
00:13:34,500 --> 00:13:36,700
- [Watney] You still
remember women, don't ya?

320
00:13:36,700 --> 00:13:39,433
- [Crow] Sand nazis,
I hate these guys!

321
00:13:39,433 --> 00:13:41,167
- [Mike] Wouldn't it be great

322
00:13:41,167 --> 00:13:42,767
if you were stuck
in another dimension

323
00:13:42,767 --> 00:13:44,833
with an annoying guy
and he brought beer?

324
00:13:44,833 --> 00:13:45,700
- [Watney] Cabot!

325
00:13:46,567 --> 00:13:48,833
(shouting)

326
00:13:49,933 --> 00:13:52,933
(adventurous music)

327
00:13:56,833 --> 00:13:58,433
- [Tom] Oh, I'm doing my best
here, it's all this sand.

328
00:13:58,433 --> 00:14:03,067
I wanna go back to the Pullman.

329
00:14:04,367 --> 00:14:06,667
- [Crow] Yes, it's T.
Lawrence, night at the Pullman.

330
00:14:06,667 --> 00:14:09,800
- [Tom] I am confident
that I am secure.

331
00:14:16,767 --> 00:14:19,333
You, you sit and you stay.

332
00:14:20,967 --> 00:14:22,800
- [Crow] They're
wearing dance belts.

333
00:14:25,900 --> 00:14:27,467
- [Tom] Well I hope you like it,

334
00:14:27,467 --> 00:14:30,167
oh, hey, I was trying to play!

335
00:14:30,167 --> 00:14:31,967
- [Mike] Sold with a
gel pack and a stunt man

336
00:14:31,967 --> 00:14:33,067
all for $1.25.

337
00:14:35,767 --> 00:14:37,033
- [Crow] Hey, did Rick say

338
00:14:37,033 --> 00:14:38,500
you could use his
sword to kill us?

339
00:14:38,500 --> 00:14:41,033
- [Tom] Oh, he should've
set his purse down.

340
00:14:41,033 --> 00:14:46,033
- [Mike] Hey, thanks for
setting up my stunt man.

341
00:14:46,767 --> 00:14:50,500
Oh, stunt misfire.

342
00:14:54,800 --> 00:14:56,333
Stinky pit.

343
00:14:56,333 --> 00:14:58,933
(upbeat music)

344
00:15:03,267 --> 00:15:04,667
- [Mike] He's all
yours, take him.

345
00:15:04,667 --> 00:15:05,767
- [Crow] Yes, take
him, take him.

346
00:15:05,767 --> 00:15:09,300
Hey, it's a gallon bike tights.

347
00:15:09,300 --> 00:15:10,700
Bludgeoning the sand.

348
00:15:13,167 --> 00:15:15,100
- [Tom] You are in
such trouble young man.

349
00:15:16,967 --> 00:15:17,967
- [Crow] I'm a monge.

350
00:15:19,367 --> 00:15:21,367
- [Actor] Through the home
stone I have succeeded

351
00:15:21,367 --> 00:15:23,400
and Cabot is here on Gor.

352
00:15:23,400 --> 00:15:24,600
- [Tom] Wow, his
lips don't even move.

353
00:15:24,600 --> 00:15:29,433
- [Actor] The casino
has acquired much power

354
00:15:29,433 --> 00:15:30,600
and hungers for more.

355
00:15:30,600 --> 00:15:31,433
- [Tom] Ta-da.

356
00:15:32,567 --> 00:15:36,267
- What are you doing?

357
00:15:36,267 --> 00:15:38,267
- [Crow] Drying my
hands, then the towels.

358
00:15:38,267 --> 00:15:41,600
- I have been
cleaning and adjusting

359
00:15:41,600 --> 00:15:43,200
the vibrations of
the home stone.

360
00:15:43,200 --> 00:15:45,367
- And I'm out of Pine Sol.

361
00:15:46,600 --> 00:15:48,233
- [Tom] Well, she's all yours.

362
00:15:48,233 --> 00:15:50,867
If it's cold just
keep the peddle down
when you start it up.

363
00:15:50,867 --> 00:15:52,367
Have fun.

364
00:15:52,367 --> 00:15:57,367
- [Crow] Hmm, what do you know,
he crapped bigger than me.

365
00:15:58,233 --> 00:15:59,533
- [Tom] Hey Crow, I think I know

366
00:15:59,533 --> 00:16:00,667
where you're going with that,

367
00:16:00,667 --> 00:16:02,000
and enough, let's stop there.

368
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:04,033
Yes, but is it art?

369
00:16:05,867 --> 00:16:08,167
Go ahead and touch it, go ahead.

370
00:16:08,167 --> 00:16:10,800
Ahh, the Golden
days, before sewers.

371
00:16:11,700 --> 00:16:14,467
Hey Buffy and Jody.

372
00:16:15,900 --> 00:16:20,533
We come over to the Jericho
once a year for this sale.

373
00:16:20,533 --> 00:16:23,533
- [Crow] It's Iowa!

374
00:16:23,533 --> 00:16:25,133
- [Mike] Oh for crying out loud.

375
00:16:25,133 --> 00:16:27,000
Staying at a Red Roof Inn.

376
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:30,500
- [Tom] Oh, this
shovel is heavy.

377
00:16:30,500 --> 00:16:35,500
- [Crow] He's got a
Jennifer Beal shirt on.

378
00:16:35,500 --> 00:16:36,900
- [Mike] Hi Cabot, there's
something you haven't told me.

379
00:16:36,900 --> 00:16:38,200
Quite a lot.

380
00:16:38,200 --> 00:16:39,500
Who are you?

381
00:16:39,500 --> 00:16:40,633
- [Actor] My name is Cabot.

382
00:16:40,633 --> 00:16:42,100
- [Tom] Cabot?

383
00:16:42,100 --> 00:16:43,067
- [Actor] Cabot!

384
00:16:43,067 --> 00:16:43,933
- [Actor] Cabot!

385
00:16:43,933 --> 00:16:44,800
- [Actor] Cabot!

386
00:16:44,800 --> 00:16:45,967
- [Actor] Cabot?

387
00:16:45,967 --> 00:16:47,100
- [Mike] Nope,
doesn't ring a bell.

388
00:16:47,100 --> 00:16:48,567
- [Actor] I'm
looking for Marlenus.

389
00:16:48,567 --> 00:16:49,233
- [Mike] Marlenus' castle
is just down the road,

390
00:16:49,233 --> 00:16:50,400
follow the road.

391
00:16:50,400 --> 00:16:51,200
- [Tom] Strut,
pout, point it out,

392
00:16:51,200 --> 00:16:52,100
what you want from me?

393
00:16:54,333 --> 00:16:56,100
- [Crow] Whoa-ho
that's real butt!

394
00:16:56,100 --> 00:17:01,100
- [Watney] I'm with
him, we're like this.

395
00:17:02,500 --> 00:17:04,800
- [Mike] It's like being
welcome by the cast of Fame.

396
00:17:04,800 --> 00:17:06,733
- [Tom] Harvey, must you
always bring your work home

397
00:17:06,733 --> 00:17:07,967
from the office?

398
00:17:07,967 --> 00:17:09,267
- [Actor] Darling,
what's the fuss?

399
00:17:09,267 --> 00:17:11,100
- [Tom] Tell me
what's happening.

400
00:17:11,100 --> 00:17:14,700
- [Actor] It's Cabot, he has
returned from his world to us.

401
00:17:14,700 --> 00:17:15,933
- [Actor] So?

402
00:17:15,933 --> 00:17:18,533
- [Actor] Cabot, Cabot, Cabot!

403
00:17:18,533 --> 00:17:20,300
- [Tom] So, Cabot then, huh?

404
00:17:20,300 --> 00:17:21,767
- [Crow] Yeah!

405
00:17:21,767 --> 00:17:23,000
- [Actor] He defeated
Sarm, the priest of kings.

406
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:27,500
Darling, I owe him
my freedom too.

407
00:17:27,500 --> 00:17:29,700
- [Crow] I can't find the
Christmas tree star anywhere.

408
00:17:29,700 --> 00:17:32,700
- [Actor] Koruba would
still be in ruins my dear,

409
00:17:32,700 --> 00:17:34,067
don't you understand?

410
00:17:34,067 --> 00:17:35,800
- [Actor] Times have changed.

411
00:17:35,800 --> 00:17:36,733
- [Actor] Oh, darling.

412
00:17:36,733 --> 00:17:38,000
- [Actor] We are at peace now.

413
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:39,433
Does the man realize he
is disrupting our nation

414
00:17:39,433 --> 00:17:40,733
by his little visit?

415
00:17:40,733 --> 00:17:42,367
- Oh, darling.

416
00:17:42,367 --> 00:17:46,000
- [Tom] Cabot, it is Cabot,
he has returned, my darling.

417
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:47,267
Cabot!

418
00:17:47,267 --> 00:17:48,133
- [Mike] Oh, it's
a different Cabot.

419
00:17:48,133 --> 00:17:48,967
- [Tom] Cabot!

420
00:17:49,867 --> 00:17:51,867
- [Crow] I need a bigger room.

421
00:17:51,867 --> 00:17:54,333
- [Tom] Hmm, she
must be a goalie.

422
00:17:55,933 --> 00:17:58,100
- [Actor] Cabot.

423
00:17:58,100 --> 00:17:59,500
- [Crow] So, uh,
Cabot's coming then?

424
00:17:59,500 --> 00:18:00,933
- [Mike] Pretty much.

425
00:18:00,933 --> 00:18:02,433
(all repeating "Cabot")

426
00:18:02,433 --> 00:18:04,667
- [Tom] Personally, I think
Cabot is highly overrated.

427
00:18:04,667 --> 00:18:05,500
- Cabot!

428
00:18:07,867 --> 00:18:09,400
- [Tom] So our hero's
name is, what again?

429
00:18:09,400 --> 00:18:10,700
- [Mike] Cabot.

430
00:18:10,700 --> 00:18:12,133
- [Tom] Cabot.

431
00:18:12,133 --> 00:18:14,667
- [Crow] Oh, I gotta
make dinner for Cabot.

432
00:18:14,667 --> 00:18:16,833
- [Tom] It's time for
the Brutal Gourmet.

433
00:18:16,833 --> 00:18:20,500
Ahh, good seasons and me.

434
00:18:20,500 --> 00:18:23,567
Now to preheat the oven
and grease the pan.

435
00:18:26,167 --> 00:18:28,133
- [Mike] This is my room, Lara,

436
00:18:28,133 --> 00:18:30,500
no one said you
could come in here.

437
00:18:30,500 --> 00:18:32,900
- [Actor] I do not
wish to be disturbed.

438
00:18:32,900 --> 00:18:35,433
- [Actor] You will like it
less when you hear my news.

439
00:18:35,433 --> 00:18:36,733
- [Crow] Kathie
Lee had her baby.

440
00:18:36,733 --> 00:18:39,167
- [Actor] Charles Cabot
has returned to Gor.

441
00:18:39,167 --> 00:18:41,167
- [Tom] To Gor, to Gor?

442
00:18:41,167 --> 00:18:42,000
Oh Gor!

443
00:18:43,167 --> 00:18:45,600
- [Actor] I told you you
would not be pleased.

444
00:18:45,600 --> 00:18:47,600
- [Actor] That old fool.

445
00:18:48,667 --> 00:18:52,333
There to meddle in my affairs.

446
00:18:53,367 --> 00:18:55,133
- [Mike] Are you mad now?

447
00:18:55,133 --> 00:18:56,100
- [Actor] Kill him!

448
00:18:57,433 --> 00:18:59,600
- [Crow] Oh, I'll
do more than that.

449
00:18:59,600 --> 00:19:00,933
- [Actor] What are
you going to do?

450
00:19:00,933 --> 00:19:01,767
- [Crow] Kill him.

451
00:19:01,767 --> 00:19:03,167
- [Actor] I don't know.

452
00:19:03,167 --> 00:19:05,300
- [Tom] Oh the audition
isn't until tomorrow.

453
00:19:05,300 --> 00:19:08,633
- [Crow]
Da-da-da-da-da-da-da-die.

454
00:19:09,567 --> 00:19:11,267
- [Tom] I'll set the table.

455
00:19:11,267 --> 00:19:16,267
- [Crow] Ahh, the book says
the dove should come out now.

456
00:19:17,700 --> 00:19:18,533
Crap!

457
00:19:20,700 --> 00:19:25,367
- [Mike] Huh, well the Cabot
thing has really died down.

458
00:19:26,633 --> 00:19:28,133
- [Actor] Cabot.

459
00:19:28,133 --> 00:19:29,133
- [Cabot] My friend.

460
00:19:30,733 --> 00:19:32,433
(coughing)

461
00:19:32,433 --> 00:19:37,433
Oh, Professor Watney
Smith from my world.

462
00:19:38,167 --> 00:19:39,067
- [Watley] My pleasure.

463
00:19:39,067 --> 00:19:40,500
Yeah, sure.

464
00:19:40,500 --> 00:19:44,367
- [Crow] Annoying
in any dimension.

465
00:19:44,367 --> 00:19:46,500
(singing)

466
00:19:46,500 --> 00:19:47,667
- [Actor] Cabot, Cabot!

467
00:19:52,833 --> 00:19:53,667
- [Tom] Did you bring my pants?

468
00:19:53,667 --> 00:19:55,733
(laughing)

469
00:19:55,733 --> 00:19:57,467
- Oh, I'm so glad you returned.

470
00:19:57,467 --> 00:19:58,800
- [Tom] Oh no, go easy there.

471
00:19:58,800 --> 00:19:59,633
Dismount.

472
00:20:00,500 --> 00:20:02,467
- My God, you're so beautiful

473
00:20:02,467 --> 00:20:05,300
- Don't tell me, you two
know each other, right?

474
00:20:05,300 --> 00:20:06,867
- Yes.

475
00:20:06,867 --> 00:20:09,033
(groaning)

476
00:20:09,033 --> 00:20:10,400
- [Crow] You dislocated
his mandible.

477
00:20:10,400 --> 00:20:12,733
- I've been waiting
for this day.

478
00:20:12,733 --> 00:20:13,567
- [Tom] Since this morning.

479
00:20:13,567 --> 00:20:15,100
- Come on.

480
00:20:15,100 --> 00:20:17,367
- [Mike] That guy's a
professional third wheel.

481
00:20:19,233 --> 00:20:20,067
- Marlenus.

482
00:20:20,067 --> 00:20:21,367
- [Tom] Wow.

483
00:20:21,367 --> 00:20:22,300
- Welcome back, Cabot.

484
00:20:22,300 --> 00:20:24,867
Meet my wife, Lara, the queen.

485
00:20:24,867 --> 00:20:26,200
- [Tom] The trophy queen.

486
00:20:26,200 --> 00:20:28,100
- [Crow] Watch out
for the tongue.

487
00:20:28,100 --> 00:20:30,000
- And Xenos, the high priest.

488
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:32,033
- [Tom] Yeah, he is
pretty high up there.

489
00:20:34,967 --> 00:20:36,733
- [Crow] You know him?

490
00:20:36,733 --> 00:20:38,100
- My friend, Watney Smith.

491
00:20:39,033 --> 00:20:40,700
- Hello.

492
00:20:40,700 --> 00:20:42,133
- Tall.

493
00:20:42,133 --> 00:20:44,267
(singing)

494
00:20:44,267 --> 00:20:45,433
- Would you please come?

495
00:20:46,633 --> 00:20:48,100
- [Tom] This is up first.

496
00:20:48,100 --> 00:20:50,500
- [Crow] The world's first
successful paper mache village.

497
00:20:52,167 --> 00:20:54,667
- [Tom] Fortunately this
is the land of Diary Queen.

498
00:20:54,667 --> 00:20:56,667
- [Crow] Cause I can
see your Dairy Barn.

499
00:20:58,133 --> 00:20:59,900
- [Mike] What do you guys
do around here for fun?

500
00:20:59,900 --> 00:21:03,267
- [Tom] For some reason they're
really into Pictionary here.

501
00:21:07,433 --> 00:21:09,333
(singing)

502
00:21:09,333 --> 00:21:11,167
- [Cabot] Yeah,
this is the life.

503
00:21:11,167 --> 00:21:12,567
- [Crow] For you maybe,
not for the women.

504
00:21:12,567 --> 00:21:14,000
- [Tom] This is what I want

505
00:21:14,000 --> 00:21:15,700
the inside of my
van to look like.

506
00:21:21,167 --> 00:21:23,200
- [Tom] Smell this,
what's it smell like?

507
00:21:24,333 --> 00:21:26,600
(groaning)

508
00:21:29,600 --> 00:21:31,000
You're so tight.

509
00:21:31,000 --> 00:21:32,900
- Oh yeah, Kor-u-ba.

510
00:21:35,633 --> 00:21:37,100
- [Crow] Next time you
think you're romantic,

511
00:21:37,100 --> 00:21:38,000
think of that guy.

512
00:21:39,333 --> 00:21:42,167
- [Tom] It's Dance Party USA!

513
00:21:42,167 --> 00:21:44,000
- [Crow] Hey, great floors!

514
00:21:45,200 --> 00:21:48,533
Look, they're all
built like whip-its.

515
00:21:48,533 --> 00:21:49,400
Whip it good.

516
00:21:51,467 --> 00:21:53,800
- [Tom] You know, liturgical
dance is really weird

517
00:21:53,800 --> 00:21:55,233
but it brings in
the parishioners.

518
00:21:55,233 --> 00:21:56,767
- [Mike] Oh, you got that right.

519
00:21:59,133 --> 00:22:02,000
- [Tom] Thank God for the pump.

520
00:22:04,433 --> 00:22:06,133
- [Crow] You know I
think this is where

521
00:22:06,133 --> 00:22:08,300
Denny Terrio makes his entrance.

522
00:22:08,300 --> 00:22:10,467
(singing)

523
00:22:11,900 --> 00:22:14,400
- [Mike] Yeah, they got pretty
decent chicken fingers here.

524
00:22:16,467 --> 00:22:18,500
- [Crow] Pelvis lady
moves into position.

525
00:22:22,900 --> 00:22:24,167
- [Tom] Melanie Griffith, wow!

526
00:22:26,167 --> 00:22:28,133
- [Crow] So this is
Bishop's Buff-eteria.

527
00:22:31,000 --> 00:22:33,433
- [Tom] Hi, we
saved you a table.

528
00:22:33,433 --> 00:22:35,767
- [Crow] She's really
overdressed for this culture.

529
00:22:35,767 --> 00:22:39,633
- [Tom] I've dreamed of holding
you in my arms once more.

530
00:22:39,633 --> 00:22:40,700
- [Mike] Yeah, look,
we've got to order.

531
00:22:40,700 --> 00:22:42,067
The kitchen closes at 10.

532
00:22:42,067 --> 00:22:43,500
- [Actor] I've missed you so.

533
00:22:46,033 --> 00:22:48,200
- [Crow] Hey, it's
Jeanine from Spinal Tap.

534
00:22:50,533 --> 00:22:52,700
(singing)

535
00:22:52,700 --> 00:22:54,500
- [Tom] Why did I
come as a cardinal?

536
00:22:58,533 --> 00:23:00,500
- My darling, you
are not eating.

537
00:23:00,500 --> 00:23:02,267
- [Crow] I ate last year.

538
00:23:02,267 --> 00:23:04,533
- I've simply been preoccupied.

539
00:23:04,533 --> 00:23:07,400
It is truly a time
of great celebration.

540
00:23:07,400 --> 00:23:09,033
- I'm so glad to see
Marlenus happy again.

541
00:23:09,033 --> 00:23:12,333
- [Tom] Oh cripes, you
don't know the half of it.

542
00:23:13,467 --> 00:23:17,133
- You don't seem
very happy about it.

543
00:23:17,133 --> 00:23:19,400
- Thank you, darling.

544
00:23:19,400 --> 00:23:22,500
- [Crow] I better go say
hello to the Petersons.

545
00:23:22,500 --> 00:23:24,667
(singing)

546
00:23:25,867 --> 00:23:28,067
- [Tom] You have to
stop the insanity.

547
00:23:40,367 --> 00:23:43,033
(doors closing)

548
00:23:52,633 --> 00:23:54,400
- Mike, we admire you immensely.

549
00:23:54,400 --> 00:23:55,833
- Why, thank you.

550
00:23:55,833 --> 00:23:57,633
- And it's due almost entirely
to your acting career.

551
00:23:58,933 --> 00:24:00,533
- Yes, well I have.

552
00:24:01,600 --> 00:24:02,467
- Must be some great memories.

553
00:24:02,467 --> 00:24:03,933
- You mentioned Hamlet.

554
00:24:03,933 --> 00:24:05,333
- Mike, do us a favor and
lead us through those memories

555
00:24:05,333 --> 00:24:07,933
with the help of this scrapbook
we found under your bed.

556
00:24:07,933 --> 00:24:10,800
- Oh, you did find it, great.

557
00:24:12,233 --> 00:24:14,967
This is old stuff, nobody
would be interested in this.

558
00:24:14,967 --> 00:24:15,900
- Come on.

559
00:24:15,900 --> 00:24:17,067
- They're old production stills.

560
00:24:17,067 --> 00:24:19,533
- Bring it in.

561
00:24:19,533 --> 00:24:21,867
- What's the first
one there, Mike?

562
00:24:21,867 --> 00:24:24,200
- Well this first
one is HMS Pinafore.

563
00:24:25,333 --> 00:24:26,633
- [Crow] Cute sailor suit.

564
00:24:28,033 --> 00:24:30,933
- [Mike] I'm the lovable
Stewpot in South Pacific there.

565
00:24:30,933 --> 00:24:32,133
- [Tom] Oh, that's marvelous.

566
00:24:32,133 --> 00:24:33,700
- [Mike] Here's Anything
Goes Billy Crocker.

567
00:24:33,700 --> 00:24:35,200
Oh, the musical Moby Dick.

568
00:24:36,600 --> 00:24:37,800
- [Tom] A lot of sailor
suits early in your career.

569
00:24:37,800 --> 00:24:39,933
- [Mike] There's
Death of a Salesman.

570
00:24:40,900 --> 00:24:41,967
And Hair of the Wind.

571
00:24:42,867 --> 00:24:44,533
Waiting for Godot.

572
00:24:44,533 --> 00:24:45,367
That was a very good Godot.

573
00:24:47,000 --> 00:24:48,100
There's the Hamlet.

574
00:24:48,100 --> 00:24:49,967
- [Crow] That's Hamlet?

575
00:24:49,967 --> 00:24:51,433
- [Mike] Yeah,
you see the skull?

576
00:24:51,433 --> 00:24:52,900
Moon River anthology.

577
00:24:53,933 --> 00:24:55,267
Night Wander, great production.

578
00:24:55,267 --> 00:24:57,633
Murder in a Cathedral.

579
00:24:57,633 --> 00:24:59,100
- [Crow] Mike, Mike, Mike.

580
00:24:59,100 --> 00:25:00,400
- What?

581
00:25:00,400 --> 00:25:01,800
- You're always
in a sailor suit.

582
00:25:01,800 --> 00:25:02,900
- Always.

583
00:25:02,900 --> 00:25:04,133
- Always.

584
00:25:04,133 --> 00:25:07,167
- Holy cow, I am in
sailor suit a lot.

585
00:25:07,167 --> 00:25:08,867
- Well you look good
in a sailor suit.

586
00:25:08,867 --> 00:25:10,967
- But how did this happen?

587
00:25:10,967 --> 00:25:12,500
- Well don't worry about it.

588
00:25:12,500 --> 00:25:14,000
- Well sailor suits
are comfortable, right?

589
00:25:14,000 --> 00:25:15,633
- Certainly sailors
seem to like it.

590
00:25:15,633 --> 00:25:17,133
- Well, yeah.

591
00:25:17,133 --> 00:25:18,833
- Wilshire the Third, I'm
in a sailor suit there.

592
00:25:18,833 --> 00:25:20,700
Oh Calcutta.

593
00:25:20,700 --> 00:25:21,533
- Whoa, that's naughty.

594
00:25:21,533 --> 00:25:22,900
- What?

595
00:25:22,900 --> 00:25:23,867
- No, don't look at that.

596
00:25:23,867 --> 00:25:24,733
That's not for you.

597
00:25:24,733 --> 00:25:26,667
(chattering)

598
00:25:26,667 --> 00:25:27,833
We'll be right back.

599
00:25:27,833 --> 00:25:30,833
(adventurous music)

600
00:25:37,600 --> 00:25:39,367
- [Tom] Can't explain
it, I don't know.

601
00:25:39,367 --> 00:25:41,967
- Something about
Lara I don't like.

602
00:25:41,967 --> 00:25:43,300
- [Tom] What's not to like?

603
00:25:43,300 --> 00:25:45,700
(growling)

604
00:25:45,700 --> 00:25:48,867
- [Crow] Look at my
split-top, butter-top hat.

605
00:25:50,167 --> 00:25:52,133
- Those priest kings
are very dangerous.

606
00:25:52,133 --> 00:25:53,467
- [Tom] Especially
with them hats.

607
00:25:53,467 --> 00:25:55,733
- They have unknown powers.

608
00:25:57,133 --> 00:25:59,433
- [Actor] Our honored
guest has no drink.

609
00:25:59,433 --> 00:26:00,300
- Your highness.

610
00:26:00,300 --> 00:26:02,967
- [Tom] Your hotness.

611
00:26:02,967 --> 00:26:07,967
- So, Watley Smith, does
our world please you?

612
00:26:08,567 --> 00:26:11,033
- Oh, extremely.

613
00:26:11,033 --> 00:26:12,367
- [Tom] He looks
like a happy pig.

614
00:26:12,367 --> 00:26:13,633
- Especially when
I'm in the company

615
00:26:13,633 --> 00:26:16,700
of such a beautiful
and charming queen.

616
00:26:16,700 --> 00:26:19,133
- [Crow] This is as far as
he's ever gotten with a woman.

617
00:26:19,133 --> 00:26:21,867
- You and Cabot, are
you very friendly?

618
00:26:21,867 --> 00:26:23,833
- [Tom] Well, we see each other.

619
00:26:23,833 --> 00:26:25,400
- We teach at the same school.

620
00:26:25,400 --> 00:26:30,400
- Hey, I came from far
away for your smile.

621
00:26:31,333 --> 00:26:32,300
- [Tom] I have a
brain, you know.

622
00:26:33,967 --> 00:26:36,767
Have you tried Denise's
cream puffs yet?

623
00:26:36,767 --> 00:26:37,900
- Enjoy yourself, son.

624
00:26:39,933 --> 00:26:41,267
- [Tom] Oh, hi Rick, don't.

625
00:26:42,833 --> 00:26:44,700
- [Crow] And step
and spin and down.

626
00:26:44,700 --> 00:26:48,800
- [Tom] And I'm down, I'm
supposed to be down, I'm sorry.

627
00:26:50,433 --> 00:26:53,133
Let's clear the floor for
volleyball now, come on.

628
00:26:55,933 --> 00:26:58,400
- [Crow] Now I'll coronate
the ding-a-ling sisters.

629
00:27:01,800 --> 00:27:05,433
- Tonight, we have a
very special vintage.

630
00:27:05,433 --> 00:27:06,267
- [Crow] 19-me.

631
00:27:06,267 --> 00:27:07,167
- Bring on the wine.

632
00:27:08,333 --> 00:27:09,833
- [Crow] Whoa, the keg!

633
00:27:13,033 --> 00:27:14,433
It's an '83 Pat Paulsen.

634
00:27:15,733 --> 00:27:16,800
- [Actor] Up!

635
00:27:18,233 --> 00:27:21,233
- [Tom] Oh, I love the way
Edgar Winter opens his show.

636
00:27:21,233 --> 00:27:22,733
(laughing)

637
00:27:22,733 --> 00:27:24,000
- [Crow] Don't crush that
dwarf, hand me those pliers.

638
00:27:24,000 --> 00:27:25,300
- There's wine in
the other barrel.

639
00:27:25,300 --> 00:27:26,433
- [Actor] Hahaha, pour the wine.

640
00:27:26,433 --> 00:27:28,200
- [Tom] Come pour the midgets.

641
00:27:31,267 --> 00:27:34,000
- [Actor] Hey, my friend.

642
00:27:34,000 --> 00:27:35,400
- [Tom] I love the hair.

643
00:27:36,733 --> 00:27:37,833
- Miss me?

644
00:27:37,833 --> 00:27:39,633
- [Crow] Now you
have to kiss me.

645
00:27:39,633 --> 00:27:42,033
- Listen, don't think we
can't live without you.

646
00:27:43,167 --> 00:27:44,600
- [Crow] Jeez, you
need some time alone?

647
00:27:44,600 --> 00:27:48,433
- Cabot of the earth,
a man who one day

648
00:27:48,433 --> 00:27:50,667
could be the new king of Koruba.

649
00:27:50,667 --> 00:27:51,600
A toast!

650
00:27:51,600 --> 00:27:53,000
- [Tom] Let's bring him out.

651
00:27:54,367 --> 00:27:55,267
- To Koruba!

652
00:27:56,133 --> 00:27:57,533
(cheering)

653
00:27:57,533 --> 00:27:59,033
- To the new king!

654
00:28:00,500 --> 00:28:02,700
(cheering)

655
00:28:02,700 --> 00:28:05,400
- [Tom] That means I get to
be director of communications.

656
00:28:07,800 --> 00:28:11,033
Meet the new boss,
same as the old boss.

657
00:28:12,533 --> 00:28:14,133
- [Crow] That's a jiffy-top hat.

658
00:28:15,600 --> 00:28:17,067
- [Mike] Where's the
little kings room?

659
00:28:17,067 --> 00:28:18,300
- Master.

660
00:28:18,300 --> 00:28:19,367
- We have to talk.

661
00:28:19,367 --> 00:28:20,900
- [Crow] We
desperately need pants.

662
00:28:20,900 --> 00:28:23,533
- We have no more enemies.

663
00:28:23,533 --> 00:28:26,467
- Your enemies and
mine are all around us.

664
00:28:26,467 --> 00:28:29,367
- How could he be dangerous
if Marlenus is king?

665
00:28:29,367 --> 00:28:30,567
- [Mike] Now which
old guy are you?

666
00:28:30,567 --> 00:28:33,467
- Xenos power, and
she controls Marlenus.

667
00:28:33,467 --> 00:28:34,967
- [Crow] Marlenus De-trick-us?

668
00:28:38,433 --> 00:28:40,533
- [Guard] I have
gate watch tonight.

669
00:28:40,533 --> 00:28:43,233
- [Tom] I like Wade, he's
just not a dancer, let's go.

670
00:28:45,200 --> 00:28:46,433
- I needed you sooner.

671
00:28:46,433 --> 00:28:50,100
but the plans were not
in the proper position.

672
00:28:50,100 --> 00:28:51,300
- [Crow] Your pants?

673
00:28:51,300 --> 00:28:52,100
- Then I summoned
you through the power

674
00:28:52,100 --> 00:28:53,767
of the home stone.

675
00:28:53,767 --> 00:28:55,100
- [Mike] The home stone, huh?

676
00:28:55,100 --> 00:28:57,600
- Protect the throne.

677
00:28:57,600 --> 00:28:59,633
And the freedom of
the people of Koruba

678
00:28:59,633 --> 00:29:00,933
and the home stone.

679
00:29:00,933 --> 00:29:03,167
You will inherit my powers.

680
00:29:03,167 --> 00:29:04,767
- You will always guide me.

681
00:29:04,767 --> 00:29:06,933
- [Crow] Touch me again, you
pull back a bloody stump, kid.

682
00:29:06,933 --> 00:29:08,467
- You will guide me.

683
00:29:08,467 --> 00:29:11,567
- Yes, of course.

684
00:29:11,567 --> 00:29:14,033
- [Tom] $200 a day plus
expenses, naturally.

685
00:29:16,933 --> 00:29:19,800
Maybe we should keep
interviewing for
this king position.

686
00:29:21,433 --> 00:29:23,700
- [Crow] My, my,
my, my Mitchell.

687
00:29:26,100 --> 00:29:27,400
- [Tom] Who's leg is that?

688
00:29:30,933 --> 00:29:33,633
This weekend package, it
was a great idea, honey.

689
00:29:37,800 --> 00:29:40,433
- [Mike] That was love
of an epic proportion.

690
00:29:40,433 --> 00:29:43,300
- [Crow] Let's watch Letterman.

691
00:29:45,200 --> 00:29:46,467
- [Tom] Honey, could you
shovel over a little?

692
00:29:46,467 --> 00:29:48,067
I don't have a lot of room here.

693
00:29:49,533 --> 00:29:52,133
- [Crow] First we baste him
in real creamery butter.

694
00:29:56,000 --> 00:29:57,200
(clapping)

695
00:29:57,200 --> 00:29:58,733
- [Tom] Deep in
the heart of Texas.

696
00:30:02,800 --> 00:30:04,400
- Tell me Watney,

697
00:30:04,400 --> 00:30:06,700
would you like to
share my power with me?

698
00:30:06,700 --> 00:30:08,700
- [Tom] Oh Jeez, she's trying

699
00:30:08,700 --> 00:30:09,633
to sleep her way to the bottom.

700
00:30:09,633 --> 00:30:11,433
- If I stay as wife to Marlenus,

701
00:30:11,433 --> 00:30:13,800
the kingdom will
decend to Talena.

702
00:30:13,800 --> 00:30:15,500
And from the way things look,

703
00:30:15,500 --> 00:30:18,400
she'll be joined by
that fool, Cabot.

704
00:30:18,400 --> 00:30:20,500
- [Crow] He's been marinated.

705
00:30:20,500 --> 00:30:21,333
- He's, he's, he's
an absolute fool.

706
00:30:21,333 --> 00:30:23,800
- True, true but you.

707
00:30:23,800 --> 00:30:26,333
- [Mike] I think even that
guy's bones are fleshy.

708
00:30:26,333 --> 00:30:28,600
- Mmm, you can be a master.

709
00:30:29,767 --> 00:30:32,433
- Are you making me an offer?

710
00:30:32,433 --> 00:30:36,833
- Tell me, how do they
make love on your planet?

711
00:30:36,833 --> 00:30:38,833
Is it very different from ours?

712
00:30:38,833 --> 00:30:41,000
- [Tom] Well I'm speaking
hypothetically, of course.

713
00:30:41,000 --> 00:30:42,633
- I would like to find out.

714
00:30:42,633 --> 00:30:44,367
- So would I.

715
00:30:44,367 --> 00:30:46,567
- [Tom] Mmm, you smell
like comic books.

716
00:30:48,667 --> 00:30:49,600
- [Crow] It's over.

717
00:30:52,333 --> 00:30:55,033
- Well okay, I've
made up my mind.

718
00:30:55,033 --> 00:30:56,900
I'm gonna ask her
tonight to marry me.

719
00:30:56,900 --> 00:30:58,133
- Tonight?

720
00:30:58,133 --> 00:30:59,433
- [Crow] Help me
choose my trousseau.

721
00:31:02,433 --> 00:31:04,367
- Do you think she will accept?

722
00:31:04,367 --> 00:31:07,667
- I don't know, she's
really something, isn't she?

723
00:31:10,400 --> 00:31:11,500
- [Crow] She's got hams?

724
00:31:11,500 --> 00:31:14,333
- Yeah, marriage, I don't know,

725
00:31:14,333 --> 00:31:16,100
but I love her, I really do.

726
00:31:19,233 --> 00:31:21,933
- [Tom] Whoa, a woman
could sublet that hat.

727
00:31:21,933 --> 00:31:24,333
- Aren't there some
kind of rituals?

728
00:31:24,333 --> 00:31:25,667
I mean, hey, she's a princess.

729
00:31:25,667 --> 00:31:28,133
- You're right, she's
a princess, but.

730
00:31:28,133 --> 00:31:29,333
- Why don't you ask the king?

731
00:31:29,333 --> 00:31:30,200
- [Crow] I don't want
to marry the king.

732
00:31:30,200 --> 00:31:31,333
- Good idea.

733
00:31:31,333 --> 00:31:32,600
- [Tom] I'm starting
early today,

734
00:31:32,600 --> 00:31:34,267
a little something I
call the Ramos Fizz,

735
00:31:34,267 --> 00:31:35,633
I think you'll like it.

736
00:31:38,367 --> 00:31:41,800
It's the Windex that
really spices it up.

737
00:31:45,433 --> 00:31:46,600
- [Crow] Dearly beloved.

738
00:31:51,367 --> 00:31:54,067
Some plain old dry
ice for effect.

739
00:31:57,500 --> 00:31:58,933
Hey, I thought you
quit smoking, hahaha.

740
00:32:01,100 --> 00:32:03,467
- [Tom] Here, now take
this out to table seven.

741
00:32:06,733 --> 00:32:08,833
- [Crow] Hey, her belly
button's blinking.

742
00:32:11,400 --> 00:32:13,000
- [Tom] And garnish
with a dagger.

